# The Sewer Pros — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# Only PUBLIC identifiers belong in this file. Never commit secrets,
# API keys, or private credentials (CLAUDE.md §52, §86). Anything
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into client-side JavaScript and is
# readable by anyone who loads the site.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical site origin  — REQUIRED for build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bare origin. No path, no query, no fragment.
#
#   correct    https://example.com
#   accepted   https://example.com/      (normalised to no trailing slash)
#   rejected   example.com               (no scheme)
#   rejected   https://example.com/site  (has a path)
#
# The build FAILS if this is unset. That is intentional: this project
# uses `output: 'export'`, so the origin is baked into canonical tags,
# schema @id values, and the sitemap as static text with no runtime
# correction possible (docs/02 §53, docs/15 §5).
#
# RESOLVED 2026-08-17 (DEC-078, closing PENDING-001):
#
#   https://www.thesewerpros.com
#
# www, not apex — this settles docs/05 §93's www-vs-apex governance
# question. HTTPS per 05 §94.
#
# ⚠ Never set this to a Cloudflare preview host. 05 §92 and 02 §88 keep
# preview domains out of canonicals, schema @id values, and the sitemap;
# under output: 'export' whatever is here at build time ships as static
# text with no runtime correction available.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.thesewerpros.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics  — not yet implemented (build sequence step 23)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GA4 measurement ID. Public by design.
#
# ⚠ Never send PII into analytics: no names, emails, phone numbers,
# street addresses, or form message bodies (docs/19 §-, CLAUDE.md §40).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lead form endpoint: RETIRED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The lead forms POST to /api/lead (a Cloudflare Pages Function), so
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEAD_ENDPOINT is no longer read. See the GoHighLevel section below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Image slot placeholders: OPTIONAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unfilled image slots draw a labelled placeholder (slot id, ratio, shot
# description) by DEFAULT, with this variable unset. That is the preview setting.
# `false` turns the placeholders off for that build. The variable can never turn
# them on: any other value is ignored.
#
# The launch control is not an environment variable. Set LAUNCH_MODE to true in
# lib/launch.ts at launch. That forces every placeholder off whatever this
# variable says. Inlined at build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_IMAGE_SLOTS=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GoHighLevel lead capture (server side only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by the Cloudflare Pages Function functions/api/lead.ts. NEVER give these a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and never commit values. Locally, put them in .dev.vars
# (gitignored); in production, add them as encrypted variables in the Cloudflare
# Pages project (Settings, Variables and Secrets).
# GHL_PRIVATE_INTEGRATION_TOKEN=
# GHL_LOCATION_ID=
# Cloudflare Turnstile secret key (the public site key is a constant in lib/forms/turnstile.ts).
# Without it the lead function refuses every lead.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
